<div class="hub-intro" style="padding-top:2rem"><p>The 40-yard dash is football&#x27;s universal speed test, and it&#x27;s run everywhere from middle school camps to the NFL combine. It measures acceleration over the first 10 yards and near top speed over the last 20.</p><p>At the NFL combine, cornerbacks, receivers and running backs average about 4.47 to 4.49 seconds, and linemen average 5.0 to 5.15. High school varsity skill players usually run 4.70 to 4.85. Hand-timed 40s run 0.2 to 0.3 seconds faster than electronic ones, so always check how a time was measured before comparing.</p></div>
