<div class="hub-faq-item">
<div class="hub-faq-q">What is a good 40-yard dash time?</div>
<div class="hub-faq-a">For high school varsity skill players, 4.70 to 4.85 seconds is average and under 4.50 is elite. At the NFL combine, about 4.47 to 4.53 is average for cornerbacks, receivers, running backs and safeties, and 5.0 to 5.15 for linemen.</div>
</div>
<div class="hub-faq-item">
<div class="hub-faq-q">What is the fastest 40-yard dash ever at the NFL combine?</div>
<div class="hub-faq-a">Xavier Worthy ran 4.21 seconds at the 2024 combine, breaking John Ross&#x27;s 4.22 from 2017.</div>
</div>
<div class="hub-faq-item">
<div class="hub-faq-q">How much faster is a hand-timed 40?</div>
<div class="hub-faq-a">Hand-timed 40s are usually 0.2 to 0.3 seconds faster than electronic times because of the timer&#x27;s reaction at the start and finish. Add about 0.24 seconds to compare a hand time with combine results.</div>
